  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The carbonyl compounds undergo Clemmenson&#39;s reduction in the presence of zinc amalgam and concentrated hydrochloric acid to form alkanes.&nbsp; The reagent in the Clemmenson&#39;s reduction effects the acid sensitive functional group. In the given reactant hydroxy group undergo dehydration to give alkene as shown below.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0055_0b67e2d6415e.png\" style=\"width: 509px; height: 88px;\" /></p>"
